List vs tuple difference
-------------------------------------------------------------
List comprehension + a short coding exercise (live)

[expression for item in list]
 ↑           ↑               
 what to do  loop

# Normal way - 4 lines
numbers = []
for i in range(5):
    numbers.append(i)
print(numbers)    # [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]

# List comprehension - 1 line
numbers = [i for i in range(5)]
print(numbers)    # [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]

# Double each number
numbers = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
doubled = [n * 2 for n in numbers]
print(doubled)    # [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]

# Uppercase all servers
servers = ['web1', 'web2', 'web3']
upper   = [s.upper() for s in servers]
print(upper)      # ['WEB1', 'WEB2', 'WEB3']

# Add prefix to all servers
servers = ['web1', 'web2', 'web3']
result  = [f'prod-{s}' for s in servers]
print(result)     # ['prod-web1', 'prod-web2', 'prod-web3']
